    "If you are considering upgrading your e-bike for the daily commute, you might want to wait. Technology is evolving rapidly, with battery density improving and frames becoming significantly lighter each year. Additionally, the latest mid-drive motors are finally hitting an accessible price point. Unless your current bike is failing or can no longer handle your hills safely, holding out for the next cycle of releases ensures you get the most range for your buck without overpaying for outdated tech."

